The function is already a single minimal call into the out-of-line `SetFieldUINT16Value`, so I kept the body byte-identical—this guarantees exact behavior and cannot be slower (no safe local optimization exists without the base-class internals).

```cpp
    void SetMessageIndex(FIT_MESSAGE_INDEX messageIndex)
    {
        SetFieldUINT16Value(254, messageIndex, 0, FIT_SUBFIELD_INDEX_MAIN_FIELD);
    }
```